{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775255094-VCVwSFAymKsqgBm5WPop","role":"assistant","created":1775255109,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me break down this task:\n\n1. I need to find the ratio of U.S. Treasury's total outstanding public marketable interest-bearing securities as of ownership survey data recorded on January 31, 1964\n2. Convert this to INR for 1965 to 1964 ratio\n3. Compare with ratio of 1966 to 1965\n4. Use annual average USD/INR exchange rate for corresponding years\n5. Calculate absolute difference between these ratios\n6. Round to 4 decimal places\n\nLet me first understand what data I need:\n- From 1964 bulletin: Need the total outstanding public marketable interest-bearing securities as of January 31, 1964\n- From 1965 bulletin: Need the same for January 31, 1965 (or close to it)\n- From 1966 bulletin: Need the same for January 31, 1966 (or close to it)\n- Annual average USD/INR exchange rates for 1964, 1965, 1966\n\nLet me explore the resources to find this data.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_2612eb1d1079c4e4","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"tree","arguments":{"path":"/app/resources"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
