 27 were for $1.2 billion each. The four 182-day issues were for $0.9 billion each. Average rates of discount are shown in the table following.\n| 13-week (Additional amount of bills of original maturity of 26 weeks) > Date of -- > Additional issue | 13-week (Additional amount of bills of original maturity of 26 weeks) > Date of -- > Original issue | 13-week (Additional amount of bills of original maturity of 26 weeks) > Approximate equivalent annual average rate 1/ > Unnamed: 2_level_2 | 26-week > Date of issue > Unnamed: 3_level_2 | 26-week > Approximate equivalent annual average rate 1/ > Unnamed: 4_level_2 |\n| 1964 Feb. 6 13 20 27 | 1963 Nov. 7 14 21 29 | 3.505 3.540 3.534 3.547 | 1964 Feb. 6 13 20 27 | 3.615 3.660 3.679 3.703 |\nMarch 1964\n| 1964 (Est.) | 88400.0 | 98405.0 | -10005.0 | 83.0 | 64.0 | 5940.0 | -3916 | 8200.0 | 311800.0 | 749.0 | 312549.0 | 312189.0 |\n| 1965 (Est.) | 93000.0 | 97900.0 | -4900.0 | -257.0 | -43.0 | 5200.0 | - | 8200.0 | 317000.0 | 705.0 | 317705.0 | 317350.0 |\n| 1964-Jan. | 5853.0 | 8492.0 | -2639.0 | -130.0 | 428.0 | -770.0 | -3111 | 4264.0 | 308577.0 | 762.0 | 309339.0 | 308975.0 |\n| 1964 to date | 54166.0 | 64845.0 | -10679.0 | 1095.0 | -234.0 | 4497.0 | -5321 | 6795.0 | 310357.0 | 793.0 | 311150.0 | 310786.0 |\nSource: Actual figures through the fiscal year 1952 and the calendar year 1953 are from the daily Treasury statement, and thereafter from the monthly statement of receipts and expenditures of the Government. (for explanation of reporting bases, see page II); estimates are from the 1965 Budget document, released January 21, 1964, including effects of proposed legislation. More detail for data on this page will be found in succeeding tables.\nFor current month detail and list of acts, see section on \"Statutory Debt Limitation\" in each issue of the Bulletin. The limitations in effect during the period covered by this table and the date when each became effective are as follows: $275 billion on June 26, 1946; $281 bill